<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Russian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1918 CE · capital Petrograd</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Russia's brief democratic republic between the fall of the tsar and the Bolshevik seizure of power in 1917.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917 forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> to abdicate, ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>. A Provisional Government formed from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-duma">Duma</a>, first under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgy-lvov">Georgy Lvov</a>, shared power with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> Soviet. On 1 September 1917 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kerensky">Alexander Kerensky</a>, by then its head, formally proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> a republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government granted civil liberties, abolished the death penalty and promised a Constituent Assembly, but it kept fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and postponed land reform. A failed offensive in June, the July Days and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavr-kornilov">Lavr Kornilov's</a> attempted march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> in August weakened it, while the Bolsheviks gained support in the soviets.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Bolsheviks overthrew the Provisional Government in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> and created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>. The Constituent Assembly, elected in November, met in January 1918 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viktor-chernov">Viktor Chernov</a> and proclaimed a Russian Democratic Federative Republic, but the Bolsheviks dispersed it the next day.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/russian-republic.jpg" alt="Russian Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Peter the Great · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Russia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Petrograd</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Georgy Lvov, Alexander Kerensky, Viktor Chernov</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Russian Provisional Government, Russian Democratic Federative Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=russian-republic" aria-label="Russian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5315 168 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Russian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5635 424L6487 457M5635 424L6092 948M5635 424L6078 906M5635 424L6741 986M5635 424L6832 682M5635 424L5697 681M5635 424L5808 852M5635 424L5820 533M5635 424L5521 437"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6487 457h0M6092 948h0M6078 906h0M6741 986h0M6832 682h0M5697 681h0M5808 852h0M5820 533h0M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5635 424h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5635 424h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=russian-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
